{
  "comment": "Typechecks the Node MCP server under src/agent-tooling/mcp/. Separate from the browser-targeted tsconfig.json — the MCP emits HTML as strings and has no DOM dependencies.",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ESNext",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["ESNext"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "baseUrl": ".",
    // This pass imports `@kitn.ai/ui/schemas` (manifest.ts, tools/reference.ts,
    // reference.test.ts) by its PUBLIC specifier on purpose — the MCP emits that
    // exact string into scaffolded routes. Node/TS resolve it through the package
    // `exports` map to ./dist, so before this mapping existed the pass reported 12
    // errors on any tree that had not been built (5x TS2307 plus 7 cascaded
    // implicit-any/unknown), and was green only after `nx build ui`. A typecheck
    // with a hidden build prerequisite fails confusingly on a fresh clone; the
    // sibling trap is the compiled.css one in CLAUDE.md.
    //
    // ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING, DO NOT SWAP. TS tries each entry and takes the first
    // that exists on disk:
    //   1. ./dist/schemas/index(.d.ts) — the SAME file the `exports` map's `types`
    //      condition hands a consumer. On a built tree (CI, prepublish) this pass
    //      therefore checks against the shipped declarations, not the sources, so
    //      it still catches a .d.ts that does not describe what src does.
    //   2. ./src/schemas/index.ts — fallback for an unbuilt tree only.
    // Pointing at src FIRST was measured and is worse: it makes the built tree
    // resolve to source too, which regresses this pass from green to 1 error,
    // because the barrel's public surface type-imports CardComponentMap from
    // primitives/card-registry.TSX and this project deliberately has no `jsx`
    // (see card-tags.ts for the measured 0 -> 1364 cost of granting it one).
    //
    // That .tsx is also why entry 2 is not fully green yet: on an unbuilt tree this
    // pass reports exactly 1 TS6142 for it. Fixing that needs CardComponent /
    // CardComponentMap split into a DOM-free .ts the way the tag half already was —
    // a source change, not a config one.
    "paths": {
      "@kitn.ai/ui/schemas": ["./dist/schemas/index", "./src/schemas/index"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/agent-tooling/mcp/**/*.ts"]
}
